                <pb facs="0746" n="626" sameAs="frus:frus1932v01/pg626"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51W89 Greece/88: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Greece (Morris) to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Athens</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-03-15T11:00:00+02:00">March 15, 1932—11
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received March 15—7:58 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>12. Department’s circular February 26, 11 a.m. Minister of Foreign Affairs
                    advises that Simopoulos, Greek Minister at Washington, has been authorized to
                    conduct negotiation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
